        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Concrete Driveway Cost", item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/concrete-driveway-cost/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much does a concrete driveway cost?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "In most US markets a plain broom-finished concrete driveway runs roughly $8 to $18 per square foot installed, which puts a typical two-car driveway of about 600 square feet somewhere between $4,800 and $10,800. Decorative finishes push that higher: exposed aggregate typically lands between $10 and $20 per square foot and stamped concrete between $12 and $25.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much is a concrete driveway per square foot?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Plain concrete at a standard four-inch thickness generally falls between $8 and $18 per square foot installed. The spread is driven by regional labour rates, how much excavation and base work the site needs, whether reinforcement is included, and how easily a truck can reach the pour. Quotes below about $6 per square foot usually indicate a thin slab, no reinforcement, or minimal base preparation.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
