          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "No — concrete typically costs roughly 40 to 60 percent more to install than asphalt. The trade-off is lifespan and maintenance: a properly built concrete driveway commonly lasts 30 years or more with occasional sealing, while asphalt generally needs resealing every two to four years and full replacement at 15 to 20 years. Over the life of the driveway the two often converge.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much does it cost to remove an old concrete driveway?",
