          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Small slabs and extensions are within reach of a determined DIYer, but a full driveway rarely is. A single pour of that size has to be placed, screeded, floated and jointed before it sets, which is a crew-sized job on a clock you do not control. The materials saving is typically only 30 to 40 percent of the total, and a failed pour costs more than the labour ever would.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
